{"id": "1fbb7ba3-c4fb-483a-a242-40085bc7bf26", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "**The request body uses the Anthropic Claude v2 text-completion format, and Nova doesn't accept it.** Nova models need the Messages-style schema, and the error says exactly that: `required key [messages] not found`.

I couldn't read the function's code directly because the agent's role lacks `lambda:GetFunction`. I got the code line from the traceback in the function's CloudWatch logs (`app.py`, line 6):

```python
boto3.client("bedrock-runtime").invoke_model(
    modelId="us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0",
    body=json.dumps({
        "prompt": "\n\nHuman: Summarise order 1042\n\nAssistant:",
        "max_tokens_to_sample": 50
    })
)
```

The `prompt` and `max_tokens_to_sample` fields, with the `\n\nHuman:` and `\n\nAssistant:` wrapper, are the old Claude v2 format. Nova expects this instead:

```python
import json, boto3

body = {
    "schemaVersion": "messages-v1",
    "messages": [
        {"role": "user", "content": [{"text": "Summarise order 1042"}]}
    ],
    "inferenceConfig": {"maxTokens": 50}
}

resp = boto3.client("bedrock-runtime").invoke_model(
    modelId="us.amazon.nova-lite-v1:0",
    body=json.dumps(body),
    contentType="application/json",
    accept="application/json",
)
result = json.loads(resp["body"].read())
text = result["output"]["message"]["content"][0]["text"]
```

- **Response shape:** the text is at `output.message.content[0].text`. The old format returned `completion`, so any code that parses the response needs the same change.
- **Converse API:** `bedrock-runtime.converse(modelId=..., messages=[{"role":"user","content":[{"text":"..."}]}], inferenceConfig={"maxTokens":50})` is a good alternative. It uses one request shape across models, so you won't hit this mismatch again if you switch models.

**Caveat:** the log entries I matched are from 2026-11-05. The function was last modified on 2026-11-24 at 14:51 UTC. If you've edited the code since, check that it still has the `prompt`/`max_tokens_to_sample` body. If it does, the fix above applies as written. If you paste the current code, or grant `lambda:GetFunction` to the agent role, I can check it directly.", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}

